---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import photo from "../assets/niko-martiskainen.jpeg";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ProjectCard from "../components/ProjectCard.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
import { t } from "../data/ui";

const featured = (await getCollection("projects"))
	.filter((project) => project.data.featured)
	.sort((a, b) => b.data.startDate.valueOf() - a.data.startDate.valueOf());

const skills = [
	{
		group: "Languages & frameworks",
		items:
			"JavaScript (ES / native), TypeScript, React, Redux / Redux Saga, Node.js / Express, HTML5, CSS / Sass / Less, Java, jQuery, XSLT",
	},
	{
		group: "Platforms & devices",
		items:
			"Smart TV (Samsung Tizen, LG webOS), set-top boxes (Netgem), BBC TAL framework, Apache Cordova, web",
	},
	{
		group: "Tooling & infra",
		items:
			"Git / GitHub, GitHub Actions, Jenkins, Docker, Webpack, Jest, Robot Framework, Contentful, Figma, OAuth / OIDC / SSO, GitHub Copilot, Claude Code",
	},
	{
		group: "Ways of working",
		items:
			"Scrum (Scrum Master), Jira, mentoring, accessibility (a11y), CI/CD pipelines, release & deployment management",
	},
];

const background = [
	{
		group: "Education",
		items:
			"Bachelor of Business Administration (tradenomi), Haaga-Helia University of Applied Sciences, 2005–2009. Specialisation in ICT expertise and IT management.",
	},
	{
		group: "Certifications",
		items:
			"Certified Scrum Master (Scrum Alliance, 2020 — since lapsed). Anthropic Claude 101, Claude Code 101 and Claude Code in Action, 2026.",
	},
	{
		group: "Languages",
		items:
			"Finnish (native), English (fluent) — English has been the working language throughout most of my career.",
	},
];
---

<BaseLayout title={t.homeTitle} description={t.tagline}>
	<div class="hero">
		<Image
			class="hero-photo"
			src={photo}
			alt={site.name}
			width={120}
			height={120}
			loading="eager"
			fetchpriority="high"
		/>
		<div>
			<h1>{site.name}</h1>
			<p class="tagline">{t.tagline}</p>
		</div>
	</div>

	<p>
		I love the Internet, the good and the bad of it. I see the web as a critical
		part of how our society works, thinks and gets things done — and after twenty
		years in software I still think working towards a better one is the most
		useful mark I can leave.
	</p>

	<p>
		Most of that time has gone into platforms other people find awkward: Smart
		TVs and set-top boxes in the living room, hybrid mobile, and the web. Often
		long-lived production systems with hundreds of thousands of customers on the
		other end, where shipping new features and keeping the old parts healthy are
		the same job rather than competing ones.
	</p>

	<p>
		I appreciate clean code and design with the end user in mind — including the
		ones using a keyboard, a screen reader, or a device that is not going to be
		replaced this decade. What I usually end up being on a team is the person
		others ask: picking up an unfamiliar framework or a constraint-heavy device
		quickly, mentoring junior developers, and stepping in as Scrum Master when a
		team needs one. AI-assisted development is part of the daily toolkit rather
		than an experiment.
	</p>

	<h2>{t.skills}</h2>
	<dl class="spec">
		{
			skills.map(({ group, items }) => (
				<>
					<dt>{group}</dt>
					<dd>{items}</dd>
				</>
			))
		}
	</dl>

	<h2>{t.selectedWork}</h2>
	{featured.map((entry) => <ProjectCard entry={entry} />)}
	<p><a href="/projects">{t.viewAllProjects}</a></p>

	<h2>{t.background}</h2>
	<dl class="spec">
		{
			background.map(({ group, items }) => (
				<>
					<dt>{group}</dt>
					<dd>{items}</dd>
				</>
			))
		}
	</dl>
</BaseLayout>

